WEBVTT

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:25.880
Your brother is hiding something.

00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:34.250
There have been several incidents
similar to what you were caught up in.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:37.570
Your brother has a list of names that
match up with some of those people.

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:42.060
Your brother has a list of names that
match up with some of those people.
Okazaki Takashi
Tasaka Yumi

00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:19.300
Leave this town as soon as possible.

00:01:20.110 --> 00:01:22.010
I'll find a new place for you guys.

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:23.970
You got that, Shin?

00:01:24.910 --> 00:01:26.040
No, I don't...

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:42.960
Jun!?

00:01:55.010 --> 00:01:57.650
Kanjouni aragau nayo
Don't fight back your emotions

00:01:57.650 --> 00:02:00.050
sono ashiwo tomenna
Don't ever stop

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:04.420
taoreru nowa mada hayaize
It's too soon to fall down

00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:06.190
Breakin' through
Breakin' through

00:02:06.190 --> 00:02:07.890
uchinukeyo
Pierce through

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:09.980
yamiwo hurihodoki
Free yourself from darkness

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:14.420
tadoritsuku bashowa hitotsusa
There is only one destination

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:18.600
hurueru sora
Quaking sky

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:23.940
kazewa naniwo tsugeru
What is the wind telling me?

00:02:25.610 --> 00:02:29.940
Tadashii datoka soujanai toka
Right or wrong

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:33.050
kudaranai ronsouwa
Nonsensical arguments

00:02:33.050 --> 00:02:35.540
kieya shinai kedo
Never go away

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:40.220
shinjita kotowo shinjinuku koto
Believe what you believe in

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:43.460
sono sakini bokurawa
At the end of it all

00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:45.730
hikari mitsukeru darou
We will find the light

00:02:45.730 --> 00:02:51.000
saa tokihanate ima
Now is the time to release it

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:53.870
kanjouni aragau nayo
Don't fight back your emotions

00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:56.240
sono ashiwo tomenna
Don't ever stop

00:02:56.240 --> 00:03:00.470
taoreru nowa mada hayaize
It's too soon to fall down

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:02.380
Breakin' through
Breakin' through

00:03:02.380 --> 00:03:04.080
uchinukeyo
Pierce through

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:06.410
yamiwo hurihodoki
Free yourself from darkness

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:10.870
tadoritsuku bashowa hitotsusa
There is only one destination

00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:38.910
Shin-niichan, morning.

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:41.710
Morning?

00:03:43.350 --> 00:03:45.110
You were sleeping past noon, so...

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:50.360
What are you doing?

00:03:55.630 --> 00:03:56.930
Look! A treasure!

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:03.630
Class 1-3
Kanzato Shin

00:04:05.570 --> 00:04:08.840
Can you believe an
elementary-school boy made this?

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:10.840
I-It's not mine!

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:12.780
But your name is...

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:14.980
Geez, where did you find this thing?

00:04:16.120 --> 00:04:17.210
Ta-da!

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:24.390
Doesn't she look kinda like Eiko-neechan?

00:04:24.390 --> 00:04:25.480
Not at all!

00:04:25.560 --> 00:04:28.860
You should look over your
answers when you finish a test...

00:04:28.930 --> 00:04:30.590
instead of drawing on the back of it.

00:04:30.730 --> 00:04:31.890
You!

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:38.070
Oniichan, you're tickling me!

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:42.070
I give up!

00:04:45.710 --> 00:04:50.650
Fine, I'll dig out some of your
embarrassing things, too.

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:54.490
I don't have an embarrassing past.

00:04:54.490 --> 00:04:57.790
Yes, you do. I know everything.

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:01.260
Ugh! You can't get back at me!

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:04.130
The Chief's brother?

00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:06.020
Yeah.

00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:08.170
But the risk is so high...

00:05:08.170 --> 00:05:13.970
It could be key in revealing the
truth behind these Reverse cases.

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:16.910
Does such a list truly even exist?

00:05:16.910 --> 00:05:22.580
An inhumane series of murders
within our jurisdiction...

00:05:23.150 --> 00:05:29.790
Then, two students he placed under
protective custody were attacked.

00:05:29.790 --> 00:05:35.390
He knew the murder wasn't aimed at
random people, but specific targets.

00:05:37.070 --> 00:05:42.040
Information is getting fabricated and the
truth is getting concealed by loopholes.

00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:45.010
There's no other way to find out the truth.

00:05:45.010 --> 00:05:48.910
...They didn't seem to get along very well.

00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:53.140
But would he hand us the
information even if he finds it?

00:05:53.510 --> 00:05:56.570
He seemed like he wanted to know something, too.

00:05:59.220 --> 00:06:03.850
We're not the only people
being rejected by the Chief.

00:06:05.060 --> 00:06:07.200
What was he up to last night?

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:09.460
Yes. After our regular meeting at headquarters...

00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:11.400
Nikaido Eiko

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:12.130
He headed towards the
Northern Nippon Inspection Lab.

00:06:12.130 --> 00:06:15.540
Probably to check out the Reverse
victim from the karaoke bar.

00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:19.200
Then... I lost him later that night.

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:22.640
He didn't return to the station until after
midnight. Seems he stayed there overnight.

00:06:24.050 --> 00:06:24.810
And?

00:06:25.910 --> 00:06:31.320
Cerebral and cardial infarction. The organs
all seemed to shut down simultaneously.

00:06:31.720 --> 00:06:34.290
I detected some mysterious chemical substances.

00:06:34.290 --> 00:06:36.890
I'm not sure if it's related to the actual death.

00:06:36.890 --> 00:06:40.160
It's being handled just like the Reverse cases.

00:06:40.360 --> 00:06:42.450
Is this related to your special mission?

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:45.130
Yeah...

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:47.660
I killed him.

00:06:53.410 --> 00:06:55.240
Ooh, I haven't seen this one in a while.

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:02.350
It's us.

00:07:02.850 --> 00:07:04.510
You two were so small.

00:07:04.990 --> 00:07:06.650
Well, we were babies.

00:07:15.700 --> 00:07:18.220
We can be like this again, right?

00:07:19.230 --> 00:07:23.290
Dad and Mom aren't here
anymore, but... the rest of us can...

00:07:23.600 --> 00:07:24.090
Jun...

00:07:25.370 --> 00:07:27.770
You're too heavy to ride on my shoulders, though.

00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:31.710
That wasn't...

00:07:33.250 --> 00:07:34.270
Nothing...

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:37.920
We hung out a lot here.

00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:38.780
Yeah.

00:07:39.320 --> 00:07:43.360
Dad sat over there, and Mom was painting there...

00:07:43.360 --> 00:07:46.620
And you spilled Mom's paint and got yelled at...

00:07:46.890 --> 00:07:51.330
"Calm down. You're supposed
to be the big brother."

00:07:51.330 --> 00:07:54.170
How do you remember all that? You were so young.

00:07:54.900 --> 00:07:56.700
It was too short to forget...

00:07:59.510 --> 00:08:02.810
You haven't gone to get your check-up this year.

00:08:04.180 --> 00:08:07.680
It's fine. Ten years have already
passed since the accident.

00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:11.120
It's not fine. You have to live for Yuki, too.

00:08:11.120 --> 00:08:14.020
Isn't this the picturebook drawn by them?

00:08:14.020 --> 00:08:14.820
Yeah...

00:08:19.530 --> 00:08:21.390
A Whale's Feather

00:08:26.100 --> 00:08:27.570
A Whale's Feather, huh?

00:08:28.200 --> 00:08:30.400
This was at Auntie's shop, too.

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:30.960
Yeah.

00:08:31.540 --> 00:08:34.370
The last picturebook by Dad and Mom...

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:46.410
Ryo-niichan is back.

00:08:53.430 --> 00:08:56.260
Welcome back, Ryo-niichan. Are you hungry?

00:08:56.500 --> 00:08:58.360
No. I'm just stopping by to change.

00:09:05.710 --> 00:09:06.670
Oniichan!

00:09:09.140 --> 00:09:11.540
We haven't eaten together a single time yet.

00:09:15.680 --> 00:09:19.550
That's all from Tanaka at
the Ayanagi Tulip Square!

00:09:20.420 --> 00:09:23.060
Here's a follow-up report on the news of a missing

00:09:23.060 --> 00:09:27.600
diver, Akira Sugiyama-san,
twenty-nine, at Toyama Bay...
I made this during the day. I
wanted to surprise you guys.

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:30.460
Diver, Akira Sugiyama-san,
twenty-nine, at Toyama Bay...

00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:31.090
I had to guess on most of it, though.

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:35.930
The Ninth Area Coast Guard announced
today they will end their search at sunset...

00:09:36.040 --> 00:09:38.900
...and continue again at dawn tomorrow.

00:09:39.640 --> 00:09:42.800
According to his friend
accompanying him on the boat...

00:09:42.980 --> 00:09:48.470
Sugiyama-san and his three friends
arrived at Toyama Bay around 11am

00:09:48.550 --> 00:09:51.750
and began their dive about 200 meters offshore...

00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:54.090
Sorry...

00:09:55.120 --> 00:09:58.060
I have something I really need to ask you.

00:10:00.290 --> 00:10:04.130
Niichan... um... Are you?

00:10:06.400 --> 00:10:11.170
Should we... um... Should we not have come back?

00:10:11.940 --> 00:10:12.530
No.

00:10:18.850 --> 00:10:20.310
I looked these up.

00:10:24.790 --> 00:10:26.880
Apartment 70,000 yen

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:29.350
What are these?

00:10:29.660 --> 00:10:33.130
You and Jun can decide where.
I'll handle the expenses.

00:10:33.130 --> 00:10:34.200
Are you?

00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:36.320
I've got my own life.

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:40.900
I can't take care of you because
of our Aunt's selfish reasons...

00:10:41.100 --> 00:10:43.200
You don't have to say it like that.

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:46.010
This is our home, too. Plus, we're...

00:10:46.010 --> 00:10:48.340
You two are just trouble to me.

00:10:48.440 --> 00:10:50.780
You have to explain this to us.

00:10:50.780 --> 00:10:52.050
That's what I'm doing right now.

00:10:52.050 --> 00:10:53.100
That's not!

00:10:58.550 --> 00:11:00.990
I'll take responsibility as the eldest son.

00:11:00.990 --> 00:11:02.350
What else do you need?

00:11:08.030 --> 00:11:09.860
...Niichan, I'm...

00:11:10.100 --> 00:11:10.650
Shin...

00:11:11.270 --> 00:11:13.030
Stay away from me.

00:11:15.370 --> 00:11:17.430
Why can't we be close to you!?

00:11:23.380 --> 00:11:24.940
Jun, sorr...

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:30.050
It's me.

00:11:32.390 --> 00:11:35.010
Sorry, but let me call you back.

00:11:36.760 --> 00:11:37.630
Hey, aniki...

00:11:37.630 --> 00:11:38.820
Shin-niichan.

00:11:40.030 --> 00:11:41.150
Please, don't fight.

00:12:25.810 --> 00:12:31.210
Okazaki Takashi
Tasaka Yumi

00:12:44.430 --> 00:12:47.450
Detective Ito Kunio

00:13:17.420 --> 00:13:19.790
Jun, are you still up?

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:22.160
Sorry about earlier.

00:13:22.660 --> 00:13:27.070
I ate some of that food... It
reminded me of Mom's cooking...

00:13:27.640 --> 00:13:29.000
Can I come in?

00:13:32.340 --> 00:13:33.000
Jun?

00:14:10.280 --> 00:14:12.340
What's going on, Ryo?

00:14:13.450 --> 00:14:15.940
The negotiation was broken off.

00:14:16.520 --> 00:14:18.510
His death was inevitable.

00:14:18.720 --> 00:14:21.520
But a human couldn't possibly...

00:14:27.860 --> 00:14:28.590
Fine.

00:14:29.660 --> 00:14:30.530
I won't ask.

00:14:43.040 --> 00:14:45.070
Were you cold to them again?

00:14:46.250 --> 00:14:49.550
I thought you were seeing them
during their time in Tokyo.

00:14:49.550 --> 00:14:52.680
You really didn't see them for
ten years. How thorough of you.

00:14:54.360 --> 00:14:55.910
"Leave this town now..."

00:14:56.620 --> 00:14:58.750
I wish someone told me that, too.

00:15:15.680 --> 00:15:18.410
Niichan, Jun is gone.

00:15:19.180 --> 00:15:21.440
I can't find him anywhere!

00:15:21.620 --> 00:15:22.880
Where are you now?

00:16:49.800 --> 00:16:51.530
You could've gone.

00:16:51.670 --> 00:16:52.760
Sorry.

00:17:02.550 --> 00:17:03.810
This feather!

00:17:14.360 --> 00:17:15.100
Shin!

00:17:15.100 --> 00:17:17.330
N-nii...

00:17:24.370 --> 00:17:25.900
I saw a girl.

00:17:26.570 --> 00:17:28.340
She gave you that feather?

00:17:30.610 --> 00:17:36.380
See? It looks like that whale's feather
Jun has, as a memento of Yuki.

00:17:38.520 --> 00:17:40.320
Why did you come for us?

00:17:41.790 --> 00:17:46.820
Plus, those passwords... like, the
lock numbers for the entrance...

00:17:47.230 --> 00:17:52.900
You think we're trouble to you,
but you still use our birthdays as...

00:17:52.900 --> 00:17:55.200
It's just an old habit. There's
no other meaning behind it.

00:17:55.900 --> 00:17:57.370
So why did you come here?

00:17:57.700 --> 00:18:00.100
I told you, I'll take responsibility as the eldest son.

00:18:07.280 --> 00:18:09.650
It's not just because of Auntie.

00:18:10.380 --> 00:18:13.150
I wanted to change things for Jun.

00:18:13.420 --> 00:18:17.650
He... was being harassed at his school in Tokyo.

00:18:17.960 --> 00:18:23.790
Sometimes, he says strange things...
or acts differently than the others, so...

00:18:24.830 --> 00:18:27.570
He wants to get along with you, too.

00:18:27.570 --> 00:18:30.830
That meal he made tasted just like Mom's...

00:18:31.640 --> 00:18:35.880
During the day, he went and dug
up old photo albums in the atelier.

00:18:35.880 --> 00:18:38.640
He was staring at the cover of A Whale's Feather.

00:18:41.850 --> 00:18:43.910
A Whale's Feather

00:19:16.150 --> 00:19:17.880
A Whale's Feather?

00:19:18.920 --> 00:19:20.890
What's this story about?

00:19:21.020 --> 00:19:25.420
It's about how all the people
you love can become happy.

00:19:25.830 --> 00:19:27.420
Hold onto this.

00:19:27.830 --> 00:19:29.420
What is it?

00:19:29.600 --> 00:19:31.590
A whale's feather.

00:19:31.670 --> 00:19:37.470
Dad and I call it that. It's a charm we
found by the sea that brings happiness.

00:19:38.770 --> 00:19:45.680
When you have an important wish,
return this to the sea and pray. Okay?

00:20:07.730 --> 00:20:08.390
Jun!

00:20:29.760 --> 00:20:33.560
I can't hear Ryo-oniichan's voice...

00:20:40.930 --> 00:20:41.920
But...

00:21:24.140 --> 00:21:26.270
Hello, Detective?

00:21:26.980 --> 00:21:29.110
Sorry to bother you so early.

00:21:30.620 --> 00:21:34.710
I searched through my brother's room, but...

00:21:36.390 --> 00:21:38.380
I didn't find anything.

00:21:46.370 --> 00:21:53.340
Omotai kusariwo
The heavy chain

00:21:53.340 --> 00:21:59.010
ima hazushite agemashou
I will take it off for you

00:21:59.150 --> 00:22:04.480
jiyuuni naretara
Once you're free

00:22:04.480 --> 00:22:11.390
kokowo habataite yukeruwa
You'll be able to fly away

00:22:11.390 --> 00:22:18.130
atashiga samatage
I stood in your way

00:22:18.230 --> 00:22:26.210
ubatte kita madaminu sekai e
and took that world you haven't seen

00:22:26.210 --> 00:22:31.140
tamerau nonara
If you're going to hesitate

00:22:31.140 --> 00:22:39.690
huriharatte ageru sono udewo
I will free that arm for you

00:22:39.690 --> 00:22:44.320
soshite tookue
Then to faraway

00:22:44.320 --> 00:22:50.360
dekirudake tookue
As far away as possible

00:22:50.360 --> 00:22:53.870
aishiteruno
"I love you"

00:22:53.870 --> 00:22:57.340
ikanaideyo
"Don't leave me"

00:22:57.340 --> 00:23:04.040
koware chaukara
I will break

00:23:14.050 --> 00:23:16.350
Stolen silver dreams.

00:23:17.220 --> 00:23:19.890
A melody kept unreachable.

00:23:20.230 --> 00:23:24.160
Tomorrow will never be woven.

00:23:25.800 --> 00:23:28.700
Only the unknown is visible.

00:23:29.140 --> 00:23:31.600
A heart of water quivers, shakes.

00:23:32.610 --> 00:23:36.740
A choking cry is all that is heard.

00:23:37.310 --> 00:23:41.840
I am your way back to the sea.
